A4: dump e2e asserts the exact capture count, not >= 1 (issue 11)

The wire-dump test indexed files[0] behind a toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(1): it passed by
coincidence whenever exactly one capture existed. Now it pins the exact contract — this
fixture run makes exactly ONE classifier call, so exactly one capture, named
*-files-state.json (the TS state is a free composition without a "source" key, hence the
files-state kind). A manifest or a second capture now fails loudly with a clear diff.

Issue closed: 11.
Lesson: when a test indexes into a directory listing, assert the exact count and filename
it depends on - '>= 1' plus files[0] is a coincidence, not a contract.
